ddress></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MISONOU MASAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NIPPON SHEET GLASS CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATOH, HIDEMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MISONOU, MASAO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIPPON SHEET GLASS CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATOH HIDEMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MISONOU MASAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATOH, HIDEMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MISONOU, MASAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A glass panel for separating an outdoor space from an indoor space, comprising at least three sheets of flat glass (G) and an air layer (K) and a vacuum layer (S) arranged in parallel to each other, wherein at least one of an outdoor-side sheet of flat glass in contact with the outdoor space and an indoor-side sheet in contact with the indoor space out of the three sheets (G) is in contact with the vacuum layer (S) and the surface thereof in contact with the vacuum layer (S) has a low-emissivity film layer (M).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un panneau en verre destiné à séparer un espace extérieur d'un espace intérieur. Ce panneau comprend au moins trois feuilles de verre plat (G), une couche d'air (K), et une couche de vide (S), lesquelles sont placées parallèlement les unes par rapport aux autres. Parmi ces trois feuilles (G), au moins l'une des feuilles de verre plat du coté extérieur, en contact avec l'espace extérieur, ou la feuille du coté intérieur en contact avec l'espace intérieur, est en contact avec ladite couche de vide (S), la surface de cette feuille en contact avec cette couche de vide (S) renfermant une couche d'un film à faible émissivité (M).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>